      "hints": [
        "Find $ar = 3444 - 1764 = 1680$.",
        "Divide $ar^2 = 1764$ by $ar = 1680$ to find $r = 1.05$.",
        "Find $a = 1600$ and compute $u_{50} = 1600(1.05)^{49}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Use the given information to set up equations for the terms of the geometric progression:\n$$ar^2 = 1764$$\n$$ar + ar^2 = 3444 \\implies ar = 3444 - 1764 = 1680$$",
        "Divide the two equations to find the common ratio $r$:\n$$r = \\frac{ar^2}{ar} = \\frac{1764}{1680} = 1.05 = \\frac{21}{20}$$",
        "Calculate the first term $a$:\n$$a = \\frac{1680}{1.05} = 1600$$",
        "Calculate the $50$th term using $u_{50} = ar^{49}$ to $3$ significant figures:\n$$u_{50} = 1600(1.05)^{49} \\approx 17500$$"
      ],
